# Multi-line yaml value refusal (review finding): a double-quoted status
# scalar with a backslash line continuation parses as accepted (yaml folds
# `"accep\` + newline + `ted"` to "accepted"), but a single-line edit would
# orphan the continuation and write an ADR that no longer parses — killing
# regen permanently. The patch package's post-edit verification must refuse
# BEFORE the consent gate and before any write: the old file stays
# byte-untouched, no orphan new ADR is created, and the log stays healthy.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

# The parser accepts the file (regen works on the untouched log).
exec constitution regen
stdout 'wrote'

# supersede refuses cleanly with the normalize hint...
! exec constitution supersede ADR-0001 --title 'Replacement' --body-file body.md
stderr 'does not re-parse to the same ADR with only the intended change'
stderr 'normalize it to single-line'

# ...the old ADR is byte-for-byte untouched, and no orphan new ADR exists.
cmp constitution/adr/ADR-0001-quoted.md orig-copy.md
! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0002-replacement.md

# deprecate refuses identically; still untouched.
! exec constitution deprecate ADR-0001
stderr 'does not re-parse to the same ADR with only the intended change'
cmp constitution/adr/ADR-0001-quoted.md orig-copy.md

# The log is still healthy: regen keeps working.
exec constitution regen
stdout 'wrote'

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
phase: sealed
consent:
  policy: off
sourceTracking:
  type: none
categories:
  - architecture

-- constitution/adr/ADR-0001-quoted.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: Quoted continuation
category: architecture
date: 2026-06-01
status: "accep\
ted"
---

## Context and Problem Statement

x

## Considered Options

- a

## Decision Outcome

y

-- orig-copy.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: Quoted continuation
category: architecture
date: 2026-06-01
status: "accep\
ted"
---

## Context and Problem Statement

x

## Considered Options

- a

## Decision Outcome

y

-- body.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

r

## Considered Options

- b

## Decision Outcome

z
